\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
I. Ontological Clarification: What the Space Contains}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The Moral Decision Topology Model is not a map of people, ideologies, or moral truths. It is a map of }{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
moral decision-configurations}{\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Each point in the three-dimensional space represents a structured moral judgement characterised by:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain  1.\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
Scope / Jurisdiction (X-axis)}{\loch
\line The breadth of concern invoked by the judgement.\line Ranging from self- or kin-focused decisions through local/ingroup commitments to universal/humanity-wide claims.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain  2.\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
Binding Mode (Y-axis)}{\loch
\line The source of normativity or obligation.\line Ranging from externally imposed or role-based enforcement to deeply internalised conviction or identity-level commitment.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain  3.\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
Processing Mode (Z-axis)}{\loch
\line The cognitive architecture predominating in the judgement.\line Ranging from intuitive/affective responses to deliberative/reflective reasoning.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
A \u8220\'93decision outcome\u8221\'94 in this framework is not merely a conclusion (e.g., \u8220\'93X is wrong\u8221\'94). It is the full structural configuration: the conclusion as formed through a specific scope, binding source, and cognitive mode.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Thus, the model does not plot positions like \u8220\'93pro-life\u8221\'94 or \u8220\'93pro-choice.\u8221\'94\line It plots the structured moral configurations that generate such positions. Multiple distinct configurations may correspond to superficially similar policy conclusions.}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
II. Regime Clouds: Stable Regions of Decision-Production}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Empirically and conceptually, moral decisions do not distribute uniformly across the space. They cluster.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
These clusters \u8212\'97 termed }{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
regime clouds}{\loch
 \u8212\'97 represent high-probability regions where particular decision-structures tend to occur. They may correspond to attractor basins in the underlying dynamical system: regions where situational forces and cognitive dispositions stabilise decision outputs.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Examples include:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Survival-driven, narrow-scope heuristic regimes.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Authority-dominant external binding regimes.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Local cooperative mutualist regimes.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Universal-reflective internalised regimes.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Regime clouds are not moral \u8220\'93types\u8221\'94 in an essentialist sense. They are probabilistic density regions reflecting common structural patterns in moral cognition and social organisation.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Importantly, some regions of the space may be sparse or nearly empty. These represent structurally unstable configurations \u8212\'97 combinations of scope, binding, and processing that are rarely generated under real social conditions.}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
III. Amplifiers: Situational Dynamics and Drift}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The model incorporates a dynamical layer: }{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
amplifiers}{\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Amplifiers represent environmental and situational parameters (e.g., scarcity, authority legitimacy, epistemic trust, empathy breadth, deliberation capacity) that alter the production of moral decisions.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Mathematically, the state of a decision-configuration \\(\\mathbf\{s\}\\) evolves according to a state-dependent vector field:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
\\[ \\dot\{\\mathbf\{s\}\} = \\sum_i w_i \\mathbf\{F\}_i(\\mathbf\{s\}) \\]}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
where each \\(\\mathbf\{F\}_i\\) represents the nonlinear influence of a particular amplifier, and \\(w_i\\) reflects its intensity.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Crucially:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls3 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Amplifiers are }{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
state-dependent}{\loch
; their direction and magnitude vary depending on current location in the space.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls3 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Their effects are often }{\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\loch
nonlinear}{\loch
 (e.g., scarcity may initially consolidate ingroup cooperation but, beyond a threshold, collapse scope toward self-preservation).}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls3 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Multiple amplifiers combine to produce a resultant drift vector.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The \u8220\'93Amplifier Bomb\u8221\'94 in the visual interface is a demonstration tool. It does not claim deterministic prediction of specific decisions. Rather, it illustrates how changes in situational parameters shift the }{\loch\cs15\rtlch\ai \ltrch\loch\i\loch
conditions of moral decision production}{\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
This dynamical layer explains:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Moral shifts under stress or instability.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Why identical individuals may produce different judgements under altered conditions.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Why reform, radicalisation, or collapse occur without invoking changes in moral \u8220\'93truth.\u8221\'94}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
IV. Disagreement as Structural Distance}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The model offers a structural account of moral disagreement.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Two decision-configurations may be far apart in the topology across scope, binding mode, and processing. Such distance predicts:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls5 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Difficulty of mutual intelligibility.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls5 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Perception of alienness.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls5 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Increased affective tension.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Disagreement intensity, however, depends not only on spatial distance but also on additional factors such as sacralisation (non-negotiability), identity fusion, and enforcement coupling. Distance is a first-order structural predictor; social coupling modulates its expression.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Thus, moral conflict can be analysed geometrically and dynamically without positing access to objective moral facts.}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
V. Phenomenology and the Experience of Objectivity}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
One of the strongest arguments for moral realism is phenomenological: moral judgements feel objective, binding, and discoverable.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The model accounts for this experience structurally:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls6 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Highly internalised binding combined with broad scope produces universalised moral claims.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls6 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
High epistemic coherence reduces perceived volatility.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls6 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Deliberative processing generates justificatory narratives that resemble discovery rather than construction.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Under these conditions, moral conclusions are experienced as externally valid \u8212\'97 even though the model explains their emergence through structured cognitive\u8211\'96social dynamics.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Thus, the phenomenology of objectivity does not require metaphysical realism; it emerges naturally from particular regions of the topology.}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
VI. Explanatory Sufficiency and the Redundancy of Realism}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The primary claim of the Moral Decision Topology Model is not that moral realism is false. It is that moral realism is explanatorily redundant.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
If the model can account for:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls7 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Moral convergence and divergence,}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls7 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Stability and instability of norms,}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls7 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Reform movements and dissent,}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls7 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Intensity of disagreement,}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls7 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
The phenomenology of objectivity,}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
through structured cognitive\u8211\'96social dynamics alone,}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
then appeal to stance-independent moral facts adds no additional explanatory power for these phenomena.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
In this sense, realism becomes unnecessary as a causal theory of moral judgement formation.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The model remains compatible with realism at the metaphysical level but demonstrates that realism is not required for sociological or psychological explanation.}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
VII. Limits and Scope}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The model does not:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls8 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Declare moral claims true or false.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls8 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Provide normative prescriptions.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls8 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Claim precise quantitative prediction without empirical calibration.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
It is an explanatory scaffold \u8212\'97 a unifying topology integrating insights from moral psychology, cultural evolution, cognitive science, and social dynamics.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Future empirical work could:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls9 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Anchor regime clouds using survey and behavioural data.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls9 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
Estimate drift functions for specific amplifiers.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls9 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Test predictions regarding disagreement intensity and moral shift under stress.}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af9\afs36\ab \ltrch\hich\af3\loch\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\f3\fs36\b\dbch\af7\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Concluding Position}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
The Moral Decision Topology Model reframes morality as an emergent, structured dynamical system of decision-production. It maps how moral configurations arise, cluster, shift, and conflict under varying conditions.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
By providing a coherent generative explanation for moral behaviour and disagreement, it renders metaphysical realism unnecessary for understanding moral phenomena \u8212\'97 without needing to refute it outright.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
That is its central theoretical contribution.}
\par \pard\plain \s24\rtlch\afs12 \ltrch\loch\sb0\sa283\brdrt\brdrnone\brdrl\brdrnone\brdrb\brdrdb\brdrw1\brdrcf15\brsp0\brdrr\brdrnone\noline\fs12\ql\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\ql\ltrpar{\loch
If you\u8217\'92d like, the next step can be either:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls10 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\loch
A short \u8220\'93critique and stress-test\u8221\'94 section anticipating likely objections from realists, or }
\par \pard\plain \s20\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af4 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\f4\dbch\af4 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls10 \fi-283\li0\lin0\ql\tx709\fi-283\li709\lin709\ltrpar{\loch
Refinement of the regime-cloud + disagreement-geometry layer before moving toward contested-topic mapping.}
